Adaptation, not byte-identical upstream reproduction: retain Sculpt's explicit
pin mode, four-CSS-pixel click/drag tolerance, hit point/face normal, stored
camera position/controls target and numbered selectable HTML pin semantics.
Use the existing pinned Three.Raycaster and viewer scene/OrbitControls rather
than React Three Fiber/Drei or a second renderer. No vendor code is changed.
Unlike Sculpt's normalized world-space position, positions/normals here use
the current GLB scene root's local space; camera position/target retain the
existing viewer scene space. Root/world conversion uses Three matrices and
normal matrices, including non-uniform transforms. Focus restores that camera
snapshot immediately; it does not copy Sculpt's camera interpolation.
Only static GLB surface annotation is supported. PLY/SKP picking and tracking
anchors across asset replacement, animation, skinning or morphs are not claimed.
The application binds asset revision and prefilters private/public marker access.
